  "slug": "contract-terms-01-mechanism",
  "title": "Clause from an auxiliary document, without a rule — the documents' journeys and the clause slip, on two lanes",
  "titleEs": "Cláusula incorporada — Mecanismo o relación explicada",
  "category": "contract-terms",
  "categoryName": "Contenido y cláusulas",
  "motif": "Cláusula incorporada",
  "treatment": "mechanism",
  "family": "spatial-mechanism",
  "description": "A time-lane diagram: Party A's lane and Party B's lane, the supplied order running along both. Party A's auxiliary document (●, a placeholder clause slip in its dock) and Party B's contract set (◆), at equal weight, each run on a solid line from the sender's lane to the other lane; only the supplied relationships are drawn (plain relations without arrowheads; nothing causal unless supplied). Then, with the supplied configuration \"clause linked\", the clause slip passes from the auxiliary document's dock into the contract set's; with \"external text\" it stays. A tracer follows the supplied traversal order; the focus element swells; at the gather the supplied configuration stands beside the key. No incorporation rule and no conclusion on whether the clause is part of anything.",
